{"step_index":185,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T04:59:23Z","input_tokens":13738,"cache_read_tokens":9653,"output_tokens":5779,"content":"Aquí tienes el análisis forense completo de tu memoria `D:\\` (`KINGSTON`) aplicando la metodología **REA (*Reverse Engineer Anything*)**, separando **Observaciones binarias verificables (`EvidenceLedger`)** de **Derivaciones técnicas**, junto con las noticias de lo que tu memoria capturó de la caja.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Tabla de Evidencia REA (`EvidenceLedger` de `D:\\KINGSTON`)\n\n| Ruta en `D:\\` | Tamaño | `SHA-256` (Primeros 16 hex) | Observación Binaria / Encabezado | Veredicto para tu `B866V2` |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `D:\\LOG_ZTESTB_OFF\\U_C4741EF2FAFB_202402050218_1` y `_2` | `7.19 MB` / `7.21 MB` | Descifrados con `UCap_TranslateMap` | Logs internos completos de tu caja (`SN: Z41220090453546`, `MAC: C4:74:1E:F2:FA:FB`, Android 12 `V82815417.2033`). | **ORO PURO (Radiografía exacta de tu caja)** |\n| `D:\\com-mod-button-mapper-remap-your-keys-2-54-pro-254.apk` | `4.90 MB` | `2EB55CF743C9D236...` | APK válido (`flar2.homebutton` v2.54 Pro). | **SÍ SIRVE (Reasignar botón Home sin root)** |\n| `D:\\Home Screen Launcher_1.1.3_APKPure.apk` | `810 KB` | `2573B493BED8ADE6...` | APK válido (`dev.dworks.apps.alauncher`). | **SÍ SIRVE (Launcher ligero offline)** |\n| `D:\\TVLauncher_4_google.apk` | `38.22 MB` | `A7417963B7933652...` | APK válido (Launcher estilo Google TV). | **SÍ SIRVE (Launcher completo offline)** |\n| `D:\\autostart.apk` y `D:\\Filemanager.apk` | `8.5 KB` / `3.55 MB` | `A6AD4357...` / `E3EC37B9...` | APKs de autoarranque y gestor de archivos USB. | **SÍ SIRVEN (Instalación offline)** |\n| `D:\\adb comandos.txt` y `D:\\Comandos.txt` | `1.1 KB` / `297 B` | Texto UTF-8 | Comandos ADB para desactivar Play Protect y `pm uninstall --user 0`. | **SÍ SIRVEN** |\n| `D:\\ADBAppControl-1.8.6-setup.exe` | `45.32 MB` | Instalador GUI Windows | Herramienta visual para desactivar apps e instalar APKs por ADB sin escribir comandos. | **SÍ SIRVE** |\n| `D:\\adnl.exe` + `D:\\xview 2\\WorldCup_Device\\InstallDriver.exe` | `2.43 MB` | `74EFF82E8B8F9EF8...` | `Amlogic DNL protocol tool V[2.6.3]` + instalador de dr\n<truncated 4271 bytes>\naunchers listos para instalar sin conectarte a internet.\n2. **`D:\\com-mod-button-mapper-remap-your-keys-2-54-pro-254.apk` (*Button Mapper Pro*)**: Permite configurar el botón **Home** de tu control remoto para que abra siempre tu nuevo Launcher.\n3. **`D:\\adb comandos.txt`**: Trae los dos comandos clave para apagar el bloqueo de Google Play Protect por ADB:\n   ```cmd\n   adb shell settings put global package_verifier_user_consent -1\n   adb shell settings put global package_verifier_enable 0\n   ```\n4. **`D:\\ADBAppControl-1.8.6-setup.exe`** y nuestro script [LIBERAR_SIN_ABRIR_CAJA.bat](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/LIBERAR_SIN_ABRIR_CAJA.bat): Te permiten instalar esos APKs de tu memoria y desactivar `XView+` y `Megacable Core` desde la PC **sin internet** y **sin abrir un solo tornillo**.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Qué hacer ahora mismo para quitar la pantalla azul y liberarla (100% Sin Internet)\n\nComo la pantalla azul solo salta cuando la caja detecta internet:\n\n1. **Apaga el Hotspot de tu celular** (para que la caja quede totalmente sin internet).\n2. **Reinicia la caja** (desconéctala de la corriente 3 segundos y vuelve a conectarla) o entra a **Configuración → Apps → Ver todas las apps → XView+ → Borrar datos** con el Hotspot apagado. Al no haber internet, la pantalla azul **no volverá a salir**.\n3. Sin conectarla a internet, ve en tu tele a:\n   - **Configuración** → **Preferencias del dispositivo** → **Información** → baja hasta **Compilación** y presiona **OK 7 veces** en tu control remoto hasta que diga *\"Ya eres programador\"*.\n   - Regresa un paso atrás, entra a **Opciones de programador** y activa **Depuración por USB** (`USB Debugging`).\n4. Conecta la caja a tu PC (por el cable USB Macho-a-Macho en el puerto lateral `USB 1` o por cable de red Ethernet a un módem/router **con el cable de internet desconectado**) y avísame aquí mismo: desde aquí te instalo directamente los Launchers de tu memoria `D:\\` y desactivamos `Megacable Core` y `XView+` de forma definitiva en 10 segundos.","thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nAnalyzing the USB drive reveals firmware images for a different model; attempting to flash these would cause hardware failure. Diagnostic logs from the device itself indicate the current build version. Investigating these logs may provide further insights.\n\n\nThe absence of standard Android UI options, like \"Uninstall updates\" and \"Force stop\", requires investigation. The analysis focuses on understanding why these options are unavailable within the settings menu. Standard Android utilities and ADB tools are being examined for diagnostics.\n\n\nVerifying the extracted evidence; ensuring all file paths, sizes, SHA-256 hashes, binary headers, and verdicts (SIRVE vs. PELIGRO / NO USAR) are included in the 'Resumen Ejecutivo REA'. Cross-referencing the findings from `EvidenceLedger` to ensure accuracy. The analysis also focuses on confirming the integrity of decrypted logs from `D:\\LOG_ZTESTB_OFF`, specifically the log files `ULog_1_20240205_DEC.log` and `ULog_2_20240205_DEC.log` to reveal the device's complete profile, including its serial number and MAC address.\n\n\nThe device's configuration analysis reveals specific hardware and software versions: an Amlogic S905X2 SoC, U-Boot bootloader, and Android 12 firmware. This pre-installed firmware version explains why \"Uninstall updates\" is unavailable; the application's current version is the factory default. The system server's special rule, marking the application as a persistent system process, accounts for the reappearance of the blue screen upon data clearing.\n\n\nThe Wi-Fi activation triggered an immediate blue screen, confirming an active process. Direct evidence from `QADEBUG.ini` indicates the firmware `V82815417.2033` accepted the file and launched the `RemoteStbCfgService`. These files (`D:\\xview 2\\v2f\\B866FA\\`, `D:\\xview 2\\v2f\\B866FB\\`, `D:\\B866FA\\`, `D:\\B866FB\\`, `D:\\mmcblk0boot0.bin`, and `D:\\MULTI TOOLS googletv.cmd`) MUST NOT be flashed. Binary evidence shows the device is a MyRepublic Indonesia model (oppen/B866F/DV9135).\n\n\nThe analyzed device corresponds to a ZTE B866F V1.1 model with an Amlogic S905Y4 processor, distinct from the target ZTE B866V2. Attempting to flash bootloader images from the B866F onto the B866V2 would likely brick the device due to hardware incompatibility (different processors and DDR4 RAM). The provided diagram is also from a different model. Crucially, the analysis confirms that no physical intervention is required.\n\nFurthermore, readily available APKs at the root of the drive are a very positive finding. Button Mapper Pro v2.54, which enables remapping keys, is present.\n\n\nThe immediate focus is on remapping the remote's Home button to the new launcher, preventing the `XView+` application from launching. Evaluating lightweight launchers (`Home Screen Launcher_1.1.3_APKPure.apk` and `TVLauncher_4_google.apk`) suitable for installation without internet access. Additional utilities for auto-starting applications (`autostart.apk`) and local file management (`Filemanager.apk`) are also being considered.\n\nExternal PC tools are available for remote control via USB/local network. These utilities will disable `XView+` and `Megacable Core` and sideload APKs, activated by enabling USB debugging.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
